          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Tutu's Later Years and International Influence</strong><br>\nIn his later years, Desmond Tutu remained active in social issues, advocating for human rights, LGBTQ rights, and the fight against AIDS, tuberculosis, and poverty. His influence extended beyond South Africa, where he was seen as a moral compass and a voice for the oppressed and voiceless worldwide.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Tutu's Philosophy and Teachings</strong><br>\nDesmond Tutu's teachings centered on the concept of \"Ubuntu,\" a Nguni Bantu term meaning \"humanity.\" He often explained Ubuntu as the belief in a universal bond of sharing that connects all humanity. His philosophy contributed to the peaceful transition of South Africa to a democratic society.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Death</strong><br>\nDesmond Tutu passed away on December 26, 2021. He left behind a legacy as a tireless fighter for justice and equality. His death was mourned around the world, and he is remembered as one of the most influential leaders of the 20th century, whose life's work helped dismantle apartheid and inspired many to continue the fight for a fair and just society.</p>\n"
              },
